//==
// # STEP to mesh: types
//
// Layer 8 of the STEP B-rep to mesh design (README.md beside this file). The
// options of a meshing run, the state of its bounded refinement loop, and the
// records the pipeline returns. The parse stage returns layer 3's ParsedFile
// and the decode stage layer 3's DecodedModel, unchanged; this layer adds the
// outcome of meshing a model and the outcome of meshing a STEP text.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Options
//  - The refinement loop
//  - Outcomes

//==
// # Options

// What a meshing run must achieve and how its result is checked.
//   Face: the edge and face criteria (layers 4 and 5); every length in model
//     units, every angle an Angle.
//   Level: how far the result is validated (layer 7); MeshOutcome.Ok is the
//     verdict at this level.
//   MaxRefinementRounds: the most refinement steps the loop takes, each
//     refining the edges face meshing asked for and meshing their faces again;
//     0 meshes every face once and refines nothing.
//   Decode: the defaults the STEP decoder applies where a file is silent,
//     passed through to DecodeBrepWith by MeshStepText.
//   Quality: the element quality thresholds the mesh is reported against
//     (layer 6), passed to layer 7's ValidateModelMesh; a threshold missed
//     is Info, never an Error.
// Plain data: a run refuses options that fail IsWellFormed, with a
// diagnostic, instead of running on them.
type MeshingOptions
{
    Face: FaceMeshingCriteria;
    Level: ConformanceLevel;
    MaxRefinementRounds: Integer;
    Decode: DecodePolicy;
    Quality: MeshQualityThresholds;
}

//==
// # The refinement loop

// The state of the refinement loop after Round steps, for one model, one set
// of options, and one choice of faces to mesh. Built only by InitialState and
// Step (and the loops StateAfter and FinalState over them).
//   Discretizations: one entry per model edge, indexed by BrepEdgeIndex: the
//     edge's single polyline, or no points at all for an edge that layer 4's
//     CanDiscretize rejects (layer 4's Undiscretized); no face citing such an edge is
//     meshed.
//   Floors: per edge, the largest segment count any request has asked for so
//     far; the record against which layer 4's Law_SegmentFloorMet checks the
//     discretizations.
//   Outcomes: one entry per model face, indexed by BrepFaceIndex: the face's
//     latest FaceMeshOutcome (layer 5).
//   Pending: the refinement requests of the faces meshed in the latest round,
//     which the next step answers.
type PipelineState
{
    Round: Integer;
    Discretizations: EdgeDiscretizations;
    Floors: SegmentFloors;
    Outcomes: Array<FaceMeshOutcome>;
    Pending: Array<EdgeRefinementRequest>;
}

//==
// # Outcomes

// The result of meshing a model.
//   Ok: Report has no diagnostic of severity Error. Set in one place
//     (MeshOutcomeOf), so it is exactly Report.IsClean.
//   Mesh: the assembled mesh (layer 6). Every model vertex is a mesh vertex;
//     a face that did not mesh contributes no element, and the report says why.
//   Report: every finding of the run, each located (no provenance is Nowhere),
//     then the validation at the options' conformance level.
//   Rounds: the refinement steps the loop took, at most MaxRefinementRounds.
type MeshOutcome
{
    Ok: Boolean;
    Mesh: ModelMesh;
    Report: Report;
    Rounds: Integer;
}

// The result of meshing a STEP text. Decoded: layer 3's decode, kept because
// every kernel index in the mesh (an element's face, a vertex's provenance, a
// finding located at a face or an edge) is traced to its STEP instance and
// assembly occurrence through Decoded.Map. Meshed: the meshing outcome, whose
// report starts with the parse and decode diagnostics.
type StepMeshOutcome
{
    Decoded: DecodedModel;
    Meshed: MeshOutcome;
}
